  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What are the various classes of organic compounds in terms of the carbon skeleton (carbon chain) in their molecules? Give examples. (3 marks)', 'Organic compounds are classified by the arrangement of carbon atoms:
1. Acyclic or open-chain (aliphatic) compounds - carbon atoms form straight or branched chains, e.g. ethane, propane, isobutane, acetic acid.
2. Cyclic (closed-chain) compounds:
(a) Homocyclic (carbocyclic) - rings made only of carbon atoms: alicyclic compounds that behave like aliphatic ones (cyclopropane, cyclohexane) and aromatic (benzenoid) compounds with a benzene ring (benzene, toluene, naphthalene).
(b) Heterocyclic - rings containing one or more atoms other than carbon (N, O, S), e.g. pyridine, furan, thiophene.', null, '[{"point": "Acyclic (open-chain/aliphatic) compounds - straight or branched chains, e.g. ethane, propane, isobutane, ethanol", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Cyclic - homocyclic (carbocyclic): alicyclic (cyclohexane) and aromatic/benzenoid (benzene, naphthalene)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Cyclic - heterocyclic (ring contains N, O or S): pyridine, furan, thiophene", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
