  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'List the main factors that control (affect) the rate of a chemical reaction. (3 marks)', '1. Nature of the reactants - ionic reactions are fast, those breaking strong covalent bonds slow.
2. Concentration of reactants (pressure for gases) - more particles per unit volume give more collisions.
3. Temperature - a rise of about 10 °C roughly doubles the rate, since more molecules have the activation energy.
4. Surface area (particle size) of solids - powders react faster than lumps.
5. Catalysts speed up reactions by lowering the activation energy (inhibitors slow them).
6. Light - for photochemical reactions such as H₂ + Cl₂ and photosynthesis.', null, '[{"point": "Concentration of reactants (pressure for gases) and nature of the reactants", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Temperature and surface area / particle size", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Catalyst (and inhibitors) and light (for photochemical reactions)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
