  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Briefly answer the following questions:

c) Is there a difference between the initial and final energy levels in catalysed and non-catalysed reactions? (1 marks)', 'c) No. The energy of the reactants (initial level) and of the products (final level) is the same with or without a catalyst, so the overall energy change (ΔH) is unchanged; the catalyst only lowers the height of the energy barrier (activation energy) between them.', null, '[{"point": "No - the reactants and products have the same energy levels (same ΔH) in both; only the activation energy is lower with the catalyst", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
