  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Which is the better mode of reproduction - sexual or asexual? Why? (3 marks)', 'Sexual reproduction is generally the better mode for the long-term survival of a species. It involves meiosis and the fusion of male and female gametes, which, through crossing over, independent assortment and random fertilisation, produces genetically varied offspring. This variation helps some individuals survive changes in the environment or new diseases, and it is the raw material for evolution.
Asexual reproduction (binary fission, budding, vegetative propagation) is faster, needs only one parent and uses less energy, and it preserves good characters exactly (useful in agriculture, e.g. grafting). However, all offspring are identical clones, so the population cannot adapt and may be wiped out by a single disease or environmental change.', null, '[{"point": "Sexual reproduction is generally better for the survival of a species", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Because fusion of gametes and meiosis (crossing over, independent assortment) produce genetic variation, so offspring can adapt to changing environments and evolution is possible", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Asexual reproduction is faster, needs one parent and gives identical clones (useful in stable environments, e.g. vegetative propagation), but lacks variation and a disease can wipe out the population", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
