  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'State Faraday''s two laws of electrolysis and write one application of electrolysis in medicine or industry. (3 marks)', 'Faraday''s first law: the mass (m) of a substance liberated or deposited at an electrode is directly proportional to the quantity of electricity (Q = I × t) passed: m = ZIt, where Z is the electrochemical equivalent.
Faraday''s second law: when the same quantity of electricity is passed through different electrolytes, the masses of the substances liberated are proportional to their chemical equivalent weights.
Applications: electroplating (e.g. chromium or nickel plating of surgical instruments to prevent rusting), electrorefining of copper, extraction of reactive metals such as aluminium and sodium, and the chlor-alkali process that produces sodium hydroxide and chlorine used to make disinfectants.', null, '[{"point": "First law: the mass of a substance deposited/liberated at an electrode is directly proportional to the quantity of electricity passed (m = ZIt)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Second law: when the same quantity of electricity passes through different electrolytes, the masses deposited are proportional to their equivalent weights", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Application (any one): electroplating of surgical instruments, electrorefining of copper, extraction of aluminium/sodium, manufacture of NaOH and chlorine (used as disinfectant)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
