  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Differentiate between isotopes and isobars with examples, and state one medical use of a radioisotope. (3 marks)', 'Isotopes are atoms of the same element that have the same atomic number (number of protons) but different mass numbers because they have different numbers of neutrons. They have the same chemical properties. Examples: protium ¹H, deuterium ²H and tritium ³H; carbon-12 and carbon-14.
Isobars are atoms of different elements that have the same mass number but different atomic numbers, so they have different chemical properties. Examples: argon-40, potassium-40 and calcium-40.
Medical uses of radioisotopes: iodine-131 to diagnose and treat thyroid disease; cobalt-60 for radiotherapy of cancer and for sterilising medical equipment; technetium-99m for diagnostic scans of bone, heart and other organs.', null, '[{"point": "Isotopes: atoms of the same element with the same atomic number but different mass numbers (different neutrons), e.g. ¹H, ²H, ³H; ¹²C and ¹⁴C", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Isobars: atoms of different elements with the same mass number but different atomic numbers, e.g. ⁴⁰Ar, ⁴⁰K, ⁴⁰Ca", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Medical use (any one): I-131 for thyroid disorders, Co-60 for cancer radiotherapy/sterilisation, Tc-99m for diagnostic scans", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
